  "note": "Nominations were announced by V. M. Conran, town clerk, at Armagh City Hall on Wednesday 4 May: eighteen candidates for the twenty seats, so there was no contest in any ward. K. M. Hamilton replaced John Allen, who retired. Polling day for the urban councils was Wednesday 18 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5: \"Polling took place yesterday for the election of county borough, borough and urban councils in Ulster\")."
